! k-point grids on a hexagonal cell: Gamma-centered vs shifted (02, section 5).
! 3-layer Al(111) slab with one H atom off the high-symmetry sites: no symmetry
! left except k <-> -k. The cutoff is far too low for real results; it is
! enough to count k-points and compare samplings (runs take seconds).
! shifted.pwi differs only in the K_POINTS line.

&CONTROL
  calculation = 'scf'
  prefix      = 'shifted'
  outdir      = './WORK'
  pseudo_dir  = '/leonardo/pub/userexternal/epedrett/pseudo'
  disk_io     = 'none'
/

&SYSTEM
  ibrav       = 0
  nat         = 4
  ntyp        = 2
  ecutwfc     = 15                ! test only (production: 60/480 with H)
  ecutrho     = 120
  occupations = 'smearing'
  smearing    = 'gaussian'
  degauss     = 0.00735
  vdw_corr    = 'dft-d3'
/

&ELECTRONS
  conv_thr    = 1.0d-9
  mixing_mode = 'local-TF'
  mixing_beta = 0.3
/

ATOMIC_SPECIES
Al  26.9815  Al.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.1.0.0.UPF
H    1.008   H.pbe-kjpaw_psl.1.0.0.UPF

CELL_PARAMETERS angstrom
2.836912   0.000000   0.000000
1.418456   2.456837   0.000000
0.000000   0.000000  19.632658

K_POINTS automatic
7 7 1  1 1 0                          ! shifted by half a step in-plane

ATOMIC_POSITIONS angstrom
Al  1.418456  0.818946   7.495237
Al  2.836912  1.637892   9.816329
Al  0.000000  0.000000  12.137422
H   1.718456  0.918946  13.137422     ! 0.3 A and 0.1 A away from the fcc hollow
